  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q5_OSInstall
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: What should you do before performing a clean installation of an operating
    system?
  choices:
  - Delete all files immediately
  - Back up important files
  - Disconnect the monitor
  - Remove the CPU
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: A clean installation may delete existing files, applications, or partitions
    depending on the installation choices. Important documents and other data should
    therefore be backed up first.
